1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Welcome to ForamEcoQS. This tutorial goes from an abundance matrix to ecological indices and a clear plot.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Open the semicolon-separated CSV. Rows are species, columns are samples, and cells are integer counts.

3
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Select the appropriate ecological-group databank, compare species names, and review unmatched taxa.

4
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Review Index Calculation Settings, then select the indices required for the analysis.

5
00:01:24,000 --> 00:02:04,000
For TSI, enter the mud percentage separately for each sample: 15, 20, 35, 50, 70, and 85 percent.

6
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Inspect numerical results and ecological quality classes in the advanced results window.

7
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:58,000
For a readable plot, select only Foram-AMBI, FSI, and exp(H'bc), then choose Line Plot.

8
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:05,000
Use Composite Panel for a compact overview, and verify labels, legends, and sample order.

9
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Keep plots focused, export the results you need, and document every setting used.
